message: "If you use this dataset, code, or findings, please cite it as below."
title: "The Disposable Wallet: Behavioral Signatures of Cryptocurrency Drainer Addresses on Ethereum"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Araujo"
    given-names: "Clebson Campos de"
    affiliation: "ZEUS GUARD Security Lab (independent)"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23136778"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23136778"
    description: "Version of record on Zenodo"
repository-code: "https://github.com/clebson-scott/sistema-gestao-pecab"
url: "https://zenodo.org/records/23136778"
abstract: "An empirical, fully reproducible study of 1,464 + 264 Ethereum wallets showing that drainer addresses carry a measurable on-chain behavioral signature: disposability (48.5% empty vs 9.5%/2.2% of controls), an interaction 'accent' (more unique counterparties, near-dormant rhythm, larger maxima; permutation p < 0.001), and 70-74% separability by a logistic classifier on 8 behavioral features."
keywords:
  - ethereum
  - security
  - phishing
  - drainer
  - behavioral-analysis
  - open-science
  - reproducibility
